    "number": 36763,
    "state": "open",
    "state_reason": null,
    "title": "command line settings are not validated exaustively",
    "body": "Some numeric command line settings are not range-checked before being used arithmetically or converted to narrower types. This can lead to integer arithmetic issues or bugs.\n\nGenerally, users of Bitcoin Core are expected to not set nonsensical values for settings, if they do not understand it.\n\nThis is a \"tracking\" issue, because basically all settings are affected. Though, I am not sure how pressing it is to fix all of them.",
